                            "num_reviews": 1998,
                            "playtime_forever": 8,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 8,
                            "last_played": 1789312403
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The biggest problem with 3D Pool is that there is practically nobody left to play it with. The game supports multiplayer and split-screen, but with an all-time Steam peak of only 7 players, the online side is effectively dead. Even as a single-player pool game, it feels rather rough, with players complaining about bugs, missing instructions and an unpolished presentation. There are also no Steam achievements or Trading Cards, despite obvious opportunities around winning games, mastering the different pool and snooker modes, and achieving high scores. There are better pool games on Steam that offer a much more complete experience.\n",
